# systemd reads /usr/lib/systemd/system-preset in lexicographic order of file name and
# the FIRST line that matches a unit wins, so a preset file that sorts after Fedora's
# only decides what Fedora left undecided. This file used to be 99-Athanor-Base.preset,
# after 90-default.preset, which carries "enable mcelog.*" and "enable mcelog.service":
# the disable below was read but never reached, preset-all left the enablement symlink
# the base image ships in place, and every installation booted a failing mcelog.service.
# Anything we decide against a Fedora default belongs in a file numbered below 81, next
# to 80-athanor-display-manager.preset, which sorts before 85-display-manager.preset for
# the same reason.
#
# A unit with no [Install] section cannot be enabled or disabled, so no preset line has
# any effect on one; such lines are not written here.

disable NetworkManager-wait-online.service
disable systemd-networkd-wait-online.service
# Machine checks are reported by the kernel on every vendor; mcelog is deprecated upstream and fails on AMD family 17h+.
disable mcelog.service
